CREOracleBase
├── given a custom receiver without an onchain workflow registry
│   ├── it exposes the pinned forwarder without an accepted workflow
│   ├── it supports receiver, ERC165 and enumerable access-control interfaces
│   ├── it lets the implementation choose its own workflow governance
│   └── it emits the accepted workflow
├── given reusable oracle movement limits
│   ├── it initializes limits and independent role holders
│   ├── it accepts zero limits without granting roles to the zero address
│   ├── it restricts updates to the limits role while the admin can grant that role
│   └── it rejects out-of-range limits and tolerance without changing any limits
├── when the forwarder delivers a report
│   ├── it rejects delivery before workflow acceptance
│   ├── it rejects callers other than the forwarder
│   ├── it rejects a mismatched workflow ID and malformed metadata
│   ├── it hands the verified metadata and payload to the custom handler
│   └── it accepts signed deliveries through the vendored KeystoneForwarder
└── when the implementation replaces the workflow
    └── it switches accepted deliveries to the new workflow ID
